From 80b9f2ae4c0c0b9abfac6cd5ce02aad443f19830 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Satish Babariya <themadengineer99@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 20:04:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add credential broker: the guest never holds the secret

The guest is given a sentinel. For a domain a credential is bound to, the
gateway terminates TLS with a per-sandbox CA, replaces the sentinel header
with the real value, and re-originates upstream. A sentinel copied out of the
sandbox is worthless: the substitution happens only here, only for the bound
domain.

Interception is deliberately narrow. It runs only after policy has already
allowed the dial, only on 443, and only for a hostname our own resolver
vouched for that a credential names. Everything else stays end-to-end
encrypted between guest and server, so the broker never sees plaintext it has
no business seeing. Upstream certificates are still verified.

The resolved-credential file lives on the host in the sandbox's runtime
directory, which is never shared into the VM. The CA's private key never
leaves the host; only the certificate is handed to the guest.
